a733: disable the pmic functions this board doesn't use

The axp8191 mfd driver adds a child device for battery temperature control
and a test "virtual consumer" for every rail. The virtual consumer is a
kernel test driver (sysfs knobs to change a rail by hand), its first probe
prints a "only for testing and debugging, do not use it in a production
kernel" notice, and each device logs "DMA mask not set". The board dts has
nodes for 30 of the rails, none for bldo1-5 and cldo1-5 and none for the
temperature control, so each of those printed "Failed to locate of_node"
and the temperature control driver failed with "device is not configed".

Mark the 30 existing test consumers disabled and add the missing ones as
disabled nodes. mfd-core skips disabled children without a message, so
none of these devices are created. The test consumers never enable a rail
(only their sysfs writes do), so which rails stay on doesn't change.

Upstream-Status: Pending

